{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 4: a realistic demand signal built from test inputs.
  A distributor's weekly demand: a base level, steady growth, a season,
  one very large order and a promotion every eight weeks. }
Base Demand=
	1000
	~	cases/week
	~	Normal weekly demand before anything changes.
	|
Growth=
	RAMP(10, 10, 60)
	~	cases/week
	~	Demand grows by 10 cases/week every week from week 10 to week 60, then levels off.
	|
Season=
	SINWAVE(0.15, 52, 0)
	~	dmnl
	~	A yearly season, plus or minus 15%. SINWAVE has no Vensim equivalent: in Vensim write 0.15 * SIN(2 * 3.14159 * Time / 52).
	|
Big Order Volume=
	3000
	~	cases
	~	One exceptional order.
	|
Big Order=
	Big Order Volume * PULSE(12, Big Order Width) / Big Order Width
	~	cases/week
	~	The big order arrives during week 12. Volume / width = rate: 3000 cases over 1 week.
	|
Big Order Width=
	1
	~	week
	~	|
Promotion Lift=
	400
	~	cases/week
	~	Extra demand during a promotion week.
	|
Promotion=
	Promotion Lift * PULSE TRAIN(4, 1, 8, 200)
	~	cases/week
	~	A one-week promotion every 8 weeks, starting at week 4.
	|
Demand=
	(Base Demand + Growth) * (1 + Season) + Big Order + Promotion
	~	cases/week
	~	The demand signal the warehouse must serve.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
FINAL TIME = 104 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
